ut freely chosen flow rates? The note appears after the table (pages 7 and 8). I could put the note in footnotes[] instead since it appears twice. Footnotes: the note isn't marked with a marker though. Hmm. I'll include it as a footnote with marker like \"note\" or in the description. Schema footnotes[]: marker, text. I could use marker: \"Q-flow note\" — hmm. Maybe better: put the full note text in matrix_tables.description for tables 1 and 2, since it directly qualifies the flow values (Q1, Q2 are minimums; Q3, Q4 are maximums; ratios 1.6 and 1.25; ratio ≥ 40). Actually that's meaningful: Q1 column header says \"Minimum Q1\" already. I'll add description text capturing constraints, and also a footnotes entry maybe. Let me put in description: \"Flow rates Q1–Q4 can be freely chosen provided Q3 and Q3/Q1 are selected from R49-1:2013 ¶4.1; Q1 and Q2 are minimum values with Q2/Q1 = 1.6; Q3 and Q4 are maximum values with Q4/Q3 = 1.25; Q3/Q1 ≥ 40.\"\n\n   I'll put this description on both flow tables.\n\n3. Table 6 — indicating device, reduced bore, AC mains:\n   name: \"Table 6 – General characteristics of the indicating device (reduced bore, AC mains powered)\"\n   columns: [\"meter_size\", \"indicating_range_max\", \"indicating_range_min\", \"verification_scale_interval_max\"]\n   column_units: [\"mm\", \"m³\", \"m³\", \"m³\"]\n   rows: meter_size as string (grouped): \n   - {\"meter_size\": \"DN40, DN50, DN65\", ...} — hmm, should I expand grouped rows into individual sizes? The R137 example keeps one row per model. Here rows group multiple sizes. For fidelity, keep the grouped string? Or expand? Expanding makes it more machine-readable but risks errors. The schema example for R137 rows: {\"size\": \"G2.5\", ...} one per model. For grouped cells, I think expanding is nicer but the safe choice is preserving as-is. Hmm.\n\n   Given \"Don't fabricate\" and OCR fidelity, I'll keep grouped strings in matrix_tables rows but ALSO could populate config_level... Actually no,