by meter size (continuation – full bore)\". description: \"Continuation on page 7 of a table started on the previous page (not included in this fragment). Given the layout (Table 5 is 'Full bore – Battery / Renewable energy powered'), this is presumably the full bore – AC mains powered table. Only the final row for DN1800 is present.\"\n\nThat's honest. Good.\n\nTable 5:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Table 5 – General characteristics of the family of instruments – Full bore – Battery / Renewable energy powered\",\n  \"columns\": [\"meter_size\", \"accuracy_class\", \"q1_min\", \"q2\", \"q3\", \"q4\", \"q3_q1_ratio\"],\n  \"column_units\": [null, null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null],\n  \"rows\": [39 rows],\n  \"description\": \"Covers pages 7–8. Flow rates Q1–Q4 can be freely chosen provided: Q3 and ratio Q3/Q1 are selected from paragraph 4.1 of OIML R49-1:2013; Q1 and Q2 are minimum values and Q2/Q1 = 1.6; Q3 and Q4 are maximum values and Q4/Q3 = 1.25; Q3/Q1 is at least 40.\"\n}\n```\n\nTable 6:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Table 6 – General characteristics of the indicating device – Reduced bore – AC mains powered\",\n  \"columns\": [\"meter_size\", \"indicating_range_max\", \"indicating_range_min\", \"verification_scale_interval_max\"],\n  \"column_units\": [\"mm\", \"m³\", \"m³\", \"m³\"],\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN40, DN50, DN65\", \"indicating_range_max\": 9999999, \"indicating_range_min\": 99999, \"verification_scale_interval_max\": 0.0001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN80\", \"indicating_range_max\": 9999999, \"indicating_range_min\": 999999, \"verification_scale_interval_max\": 0.0001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN100, DN125, DN150, DN200\", \"indicating_range_max\": 9999999, \"indicating_range_min\": 999999, \"verification_scale_interval_max\": 0.001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN250\", \"indicating_range_max\": 9999999, \"indicating_range_min\": 9999999, \"verification_scale_interval_max\": 0.001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN300, DN350, D